Samurai have always been one of the 2 rolls I'd always reroll when
I get a random one (the other being caveman).  They fit my
preferred hack-and-slash style well; but what's this osaku?  What
the heck do I do with it?  It IDs as... an osaku.  Do I eat it?
Use it to fire kabutos at monsters?  Well, with 11 ascensions
under my belt now, it's time to learn a few words of Japanese.

I'm not a big conduct player.  After my first genoless ascension,
I swore I wouldn't do that again.  It was a little harder, but
much more annoying.  But the wishless, genoless, polyless set of
conducts seems to be a sort of rite of passage.  My first samurai
try, I made it a ways without breaking these, so I decided to try
it, only to die stupidly on the quest.  So my second try I went
for it again.

Polyless is trivial apart from accidentally hitting a poly trap -
I rarely polymorph myself on purpose, and don't polypile often
either.  Genoless is still annoying - if I never do genoless
again, I'm ok with that.  Wishless made the game a little bit
harder, but it was actually fun, living with what the RNG saw fit
to provide (which included lots of magic whistles and (BoH, but no
teleport control, +oID, or ?oGD, no ?oCharge until Astral, and
no worthwhile cloaks until the Sanctum).

So without further ado, the story of Bleeding Gums the Samurai:

DL1 kindly provides 2 altars (1 coaligned) and a magic whistle.
DL2 has the branch to the mines.  Vault on DL4, but it sounds like
a rock mole or something got to it.  A general store; I buy an
expensive lamp.  Another small general store on DL5, I price ID a
few scrolls.  Another coaligned altar on 5, then yet another on
6=2E  I make a stash on 7.  Vault on 7, but still no pick.  Darn it,
a trap door on 8.  Back up to 8, a vault and a big weapon store.
I buy a )2HS since I'll want to practice for the tsurugi later.
My dog's gone, turns out he fell to 9 too.

Finally the Oracle on DL9.  Aw crap, the Sokoban branch is in a
big room - the wide open one with 5 lit and 4 dark sections.  All
stairs are lit - I'm in the top-right, downstairs are in center,
Soko stairs are in top-left.  I'm very thin on assets now - no
wands at all, just a camera, mirror, katana, and my E-word
finger.  I'll have to come back.

I start back to the mines and wield my )2HS; damn, I never BUC-
tested it!!  My only possible ?oRC is itself cursed, so I burn a
?oEW.  I also sac for Snickersnee.

First mine level is dark.  I have a magic lamp, but I only explore
to the stairs for now anyway.  Next level is dark.  I find a bag.
Another dark level.  Finally a wand - a /oDig.  And a marker.
Cool.  4th level (ML6) is minetown.  Temple is coaligned!  Nice
set of stores - lighting, deli, wands, general, hardware.  Plenty
of candles.  Hardware has a sack; my bag is holding!

I keep going down.  Damn, this won't be the game I ascend with my
original pet.  I find a gray stone on ML8.  ML9 gives another
(BoH - guess what Sokoban will hold.  After ML10, I run back to my
stash.  Padded gloves are cursed.  Gray stone is just flint.  I
explore the dark levels on the way up and get cold resistance from
a yeti.  A sac passing an altar gets me Trollsbane, and I get
poison resistance from a bee.  A unihorn restores strength.

ML11 is mine's end, with all the mimics.  Can't find the
luckstone.  Oh, here it is.  Dammit, it's the loadstone!  Now I
found it.  Bless it, drop the loadstone, and back up.  Time to
tackle the big room.  Now it's not a problem.  A couple retreats
upstairs, but that's it.  And Sokoban has the amulet - how about
that!!

DL12 - a scimitar in a hallway?  Bones level?  Looks like the
remnants of a zoo...  No, a throne room...  And Anthony's ghost -
from Hearse.  Let's see what he's got...  Hawaiian shirt, Mojo, a
bag, and lots more.  CSI says he was probably a tourist, and was
killed by a gelatinous cube while helpless.  Bummer, the bag is
tricks.  Time to BUC-ID the loot.  2 uncursed boots, but neither
is lev, speed, or jumping.  His "bugs stop moving" wand turns out
to be death!

DL13.  I tame a dog, who turns out to be a chameleon.  Blow
through a zoo.  Large general store on 14.  I make another stash.
Graveyard on 15, and convert an altar.  Move the stash here from
14.  Quest portal and a beehive on 16.  A zoo on 17.  My chameleon
dies.  18 is Rogue.  19 has a huge leprechaun hall.  Time for a
run back to Minetown for protection.  AC=3D-8 (naked=3D2).

DL20 has a large beehive.  Sink-ID =3DoSD.  A pudding gives shock
resistance.  Another leprechaun hall on 21, and I convert an
altar.  Finally get sleep resistance from an elf on 22.  A third
(BoH.  DL23 has a vault with the Ludios portal.  I storm the
barracks, and get disintigration resistance and BDS from a
dragon.  2 wands of death on soldiers, 1 of which is used on
Croesus.  Time for a stash run to ID things.  Snow boots are
levitation.  Rings include =3DoPC, =3DoFA, and a -1=3DoID.  I find yet
another (BoH.  I alchemize 11 !oFH (HP=3D241 now) and buy 2 more
points of protection.

Vault on 24, a huge beehive on 25, and a throne room on 26, which
grants a wish.  Oh, crap.  I haven't genocided or polyed anything
yet, =3DoPC will prevent poly trap accidents.  I don't like to turn
down a gift.  Am I in for geno-poly-wishless?  Deep breath.
"Nothing."  Ok, I'm committed now.  What the... shit, another
wish??  Jeez, I've never gotten 2 throne wishes in the same game,
much less from the same throne!  Sigh.  "Nothing."

DL27 is the Titan version of Medusa.  The titan's peaceful.
Nice.  Get fire resistance finally from a red dragon tinned at
Ludios.  Perseus is loaded - he has the shield, boots, a scimitar,
a sack with a candy bar, and a long wand, which is my first /oFire.

DL28 is a normal dungeon level, with a vault and small zoo.

29 is a maze.  Nope, the castle.  I see 3 normal liches and a
disenchanter, but nothing too nasty.  Still, I'm going to slip in
the back, maybe the gray dragon will leave scales.  Nope.  But a
pair of hiking boots turns out to be b+4BoS.  I make a stash in
Perseus's sack behind the castle (my usual spot) and go back to do
the quest.

Back at my stash on 15, I make the BDS into BDSM, and enchant my
Hawaiian shirt to +5 and Snick to +1.  ID =3DoLev, and the cursed
padded gloves are +0 Power, so I wear and enchant them.  The third
quest level has 2 friggin (BoH in the tool room - what's that,
like 6 for the game?  And Dragonbane in the weaponry.  Down to the
goal level, I try to line up Ashiki, but he teleports next to me.
The Tsurugi scares me, so he takes a /oDeath.

I bring most of my stash from 15 to the castle to consolidate, and
go in the front.  I play mastermind with my flute (ccafa), take
out what's left in the castle, and ID some stuff.  I prefer SDSM
and CoMR, but I have an "oR and need MR, so I curse 2 ?oGeno and
send in 4 gray dragons.  The last one leaves scales, good.  I
enchant them up.  Then send in 5 nurses, which take my HP from 248
all the way up to 249.  Ok, that was a waste.  Alchemize another
8 !oFH.

DL30 is obviously the Valley.  Asmo is on 31.  The bastard has
a /oDig.  I follow him through Juib's swamp (34) to Baalz's lair
(37), where he finally runs out of charges.  Orcus Town is on 39,
along with Vlad's tower.  Orcus has a friggin /oDig too, but I
kill him after a couple levels.  I find a plumed helm in the Town
which turns out to be ESP.  Now all I need is an AK-quality
cloak - ideally displacement, but oilskin, protection, or MR will be an
improvement over my thoroughly burnt elven one.  I tame a
brute squad of Ollie the olag-hai, Paul the purple worm, Garret
the winged gargoyle, and Val the vampire lord.

DL44 has the top of the wizard's tower and the game's first poly
trap.  Finally - I've tamed many dogs and horses by now, but
haven't mentioned any since they've all died quickly.  I tame a
dog and poly her to a baby purple worm.  (I'd hoped she'd grow up,
but she was completely useless.  On the final run, I revisited
this same trap until she became an earth elemental and then
wouldn't stay put on the trap, so I ditched her.)

There's no tower on 46 - 43 must have been the top of the tower,
but the stairs were close so I didn't explore.  49 has a fake
tower.  VS on 51, which I mark by zapping a /oLight.

Climbing back up to prepare for the final run, I find the other
fake tower on 50.  It has the portal, so I clear the tower except
for Rodney.  Paul bites it on the way up, but Garret has become a
purple worm now.  I go all the way the hell back to the mines with
my gehennom gold, but no more protection.  And I still have the
same darn elven cloak.  I enchant the [HoTel to +4.  AC=3D-34,
HP=3D417.  I still have 2 b?oEA and my marker from the early game
(0:34).  If I don't find a better cloak by the time I pass my
stash again, I'll enchant up my elven one.  No ?oCharge yet
though.  No TC either, so I'll have to walk it back to DL50.
Rodney steals the Tsurugi.  Damn, I should have brought Snick down
with me.  /oD to take it back, kill nasties and Rodney #2.  Now I
have to walk it to the VS and invocate.

I find a piece of cloth on a priest in the sanctum.  MR maybe?
Wow, another one!  1 is uncursed.  It's protection.  Probably my
third choice, but elven is #5, so I'll take it.  I'm such an ass,
I left my 4 !oGL back at my stash.  3 Rodneys on 51.  46->48.
Rodney on 46.  45->46, 45->45, 45->46, 44->46, 45->47, 45->45,
40->41, 38->39, 38->38.  2 Rodneys on 35.  35->35, 33->36, 35->35,
34->36, 35->37.

Finally make it to my stash.  Use 2 and write a third ?oEA and
enchant my [CoP to +5.  Collect everything I need for the run.
I'm burdened now, but I'll ditch stuff for Earth.  Besides TC,
?oCharge, and +oID, I also haven't found a single ?oGD, but I have
a crystal ball (0:2).

Lots of Rodneys on the run up.  (I didn't count how many, too
eager to get out.)  Hellish summoning storms, too.  I've somehow
avoided really bad ones for the most part until this point.  I get
crowned making more holy water.  Grrr...

For a stupid ascension trick, I wanted to polymorph and tame the
Oracle, but wizmode tests suggest she won't poly.  (Spoiler says
she's only 50% MR.  Oh well.)  Garret died and Val went peaceful
at some point, so I'm down to just Ollie.  Bless and apply 3
figurines - the archon is peaceful, iron golem is hostile, and I
finally get a pet gray elf (George).  I give my 5 !oGL to Ollie,
who's now XL27.

Put "oY in my bag.  Can't?  Good.  Climb to Earth!  Rodney is
bisected on the second hit.  The ball finds the portal.  I ditch a
bunch of stuff to get unburdened.

Air.  Make my way past the clouds.  Come on, someone hit the
portal already.  Ah, found the thing on my own while searching.

Fire.  I need someone to hit the portal for me this time.  Rodney
appears.  Someone hit the bloody portal already!  Damn, stumbled
into it myself, lost Ollie and George.

On water, I float about 2/3 of the way across and use the ball.
The portal is about 4 spaces away, but I float the wrong way while
in the trance.  Make my way toward it.  Gain XL17 on the way.
There it is!

I get a guardian angel.  Pesty is left, Famine straight, Death
right.  I go straight.  Find a new scroll.  I ID it (why not?) and
it's charging.  That's very very helpful now, thanks so much.  The
altar is lawful.  Hey, I'm lawful too!  Genoless, polyless,
wishless.  The priest gives me 2 bits.


